; etyme.com: the zone for Vercel DNS, written 2026-11-09 from the live
; Bluehost zone the founder exported the same day.
;
; The site moves from Base44 to Vercel. Gmail (Google Workspace) and
; Google Cloud stay. Marketing and notices email goes through Resend on
; notify.etyme.com, which the app is already set up for.
;
; How to use it:
;   vercel dns import etyme.com docs/dns/etyme.com.vercel.zone
; or type each record into Vercel → Domains → etyme.com → DNS Records.
; Do this BEFORE you change the nameservers at Bluehost, so mail never
; stops. Steps in order: docs/dns/vercel-dns.md.
;
; What this file does not contain, on purpose:
;  - NS records: Vercel sets ns1/ns2.vercel-dns.com itself.
;  - The web records (etyme.com, www, *): Vercel makes them when etyme.com,
;    www.etyme.com and *.etyme.com are added to the etyme2040 project. The
;    wildcard is what gives every firm <slug>.etyme.com with nothing added.

$ORIGIN etyme.com.
$TTL 3600

; ── Google Workspace mail for @etyme.com (unchanged) ───────────────────
@                     IN  MX  1   aspmx.l.google.com.
@                     IN  MX  5   alt1.aspmx.l.google.com.
@                     IN  MX  5   alt2.aspmx.l.google.com.
@                     IN  MX  10  alt3.aspmx.l.google.com.
@                     IN  MX  10  alt4.aspmx.l.google.com.

; Google Workspace short addresses (unchanged)
calendar              IN  CNAME  ghs.google.com.
docs                  IN  CNAME  ghs.google.com.
sites                 IN  CNAME  ghs.google.com.
start                 IN  CNAME  ghs.google.com.
mail                  IN  CNAME  ghs.googlehosted.com.
imap                  IN  CNAME  imap.googlemail.com.
pop                   IN  CNAME  pop.googlemail.com.
smtp                  IN  CNAME  smtp.googlemail.com.

; ── Google site verification, for Google Cloud and Search (unchanged) ──
@                     IN  TXT  "google-site-verification=BBDibdPX9tTYPhaDsrVgPeKBEqMiCXs8rZjrf4WbfYk"
@                     IN  TXT  "google-site-verification=cxCyQld11ghvCXM09SlUlmD1aVXzandjIVzX9EPXQlc"
@                     IN  TXT  "google-site-verification=hxgsHBmOvl9N-eZ2B67Y-NIuWG2-L0t0SZeDnTrb4z8"

; ── SPF: one record (CHANGED) ──────────────────────────────────────────
; The live zone has two SPF records. Having two makes SPF fail for every
; message. This is the one record left: only Google sends as @etyme.com.
; Resend sends from notify.etyme.com, which has its own SPF below.
@                     IN  TXT  "v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all"

; ── Google DKIM (NEW: please add) ──────────────────────────────────────
; The live zone has no Google DKIM key, so Gmail from @etyme.com is not
; signed. Google Admin → Apps → Google Workspace → Gmail → Authenticate
; email → Generate new record (2048-bit, prefix "google"). Paste the
; value it shows here, then press "Start authentication" in Google Admin.

; ── DMARC, report only (NEW) ───────────────────────────────────────────
; Nothing is rejected. Reports go to support@etyme.com. Move to
; p=quarantine after a few weeks of clean reports.
_dmarc                IN  TXT  "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:support@etyme.com"

; ── Resend: notices and marketing from notify.etyme.com (NEW) ──────────
; Copy the DKIM value, and the MX host if its region differs, exactly
; from Resend → Domains → notify.etyme.com. Then press Verify in Resend.
send.notify           IN  MX  10  feedback-smtp.us-east-1.amazonses.com.
send.notify           IN  TXT  "v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all"

; ── Removed from the live zone, and why ────────────────────────────────
; *  A 216.24.57.1 and @ A 216.24.57.1   the Base44 site; Vercel replaces it
; www CNAME etyme.com                    Vercel makes www
; ftp CNAME etyme.com                    Bluehost file transfer; no site there now
; app TXT spf (Bluehost server)          SPF on a name that sends nothing
; default._domainkey (Bluehost cPanel)   Bluehost mail; not used
; psrp CNAME rp.smtp.adxemailhelp.com    Bluehost mail relay; not used
; spf include:spf.smtp.adxemailhelp.com, ip4:162.144.178.127, a, mx
;                                        Bluehost and the old site sending; not used
; s1._domainkey (SendGrid)               the app sends through Resend
; k1._domainkey (Mailchimp)              marketing moves to Resend
; messages TXT, email.messages TXT (Mailgun)  marketing moves to Resend
; _acme-challenge.blog, .cpanel          old certificate checks for Bluehost
; _caldav*, _carddav* (8 records)        Bluehost's cPanel calendar; Gmail is the calendar
;
; If any of these is still in use (a mailing list in Mailchimp or Mailgun,
; a form on another host that sends mail), add that one line back.
; Nothing in the app needs any of them.
